SUMMARY:DIY Phone Blocker Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Take back a little control of your screen time with a hands-o
 n digital wellness activity! Come decorate your own NFC card/chip and lea
 rn how to program it to activate a distraction-blocking setting on your p
 hone. With a simple tap\, your customized card can help you step away fro
 m social media and other distracting apps when you want to study\, sleep\
 , create\, spend time with friends\, or simply unplug.  No tech experienc
 e is needed\; we'll walk through the setup together. By the end of the ac
 tivity\, you'll leave with a personalized NFC tag\, and a practical tool 
 for creating more intentional boundaries with your phone.Photo Notice  By
  attending this event\, you agree to be in photography that may be used b
 y the University for promotional purposes. If you would not like to be in
  any pictures\, please speak to a Museum staff member\, and they will inf
 orm assigned photographers of your request. If you see that your image ha
 s been used in error\, please email eskenazi@iu.edu to request that it be
  taken down.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p class="isSelectedEnd">  Take back a littl
 e control of your screen time with a hands-on digital wellness activity! 
 Come decorate your own NFC card/chip and learn how to program it to activ
 ate a distraction-blocking setting on your phone. With a simple tap\, you
 r customized card can help you step away from social media and other dist
 racting apps when you want to study\, sleep\, create\, spend time with fr
 iends\, or simply unplug.</p><p>  No tech experience is needed\; we'll wa
 lk through the setup together. By the end of the activity\, you'll leave 
 with a personalized NFC tag\, and a practical tool for creating more inte
 ntional boundaries with your phone.</p><p><strong data-ogsc="" data-olk-c
 opy-source="MessageBody">Photo Notice</strong><br />  By attending this e
 vent\, you agree to be in photography that may be used by the University 
 for promotional purposes. If you would not like to be in any pictures\, p
 lease speak to a Museum staff member\, and they will inform assigned phot
 ographers of your request. If you see that your image has been used in er
 ror\, please email eskenazi@iu.edu to request that it be taken down.</p>
