SUMMARY:Tommy Kha: Ghost Bites\, and Other Vietnamese Phrases | Lecture
DESCRIPTION:A 2025 Guggenheim Fellow\, Kha lives and works between New Yo
 rk City and Memphis\, Tennessee\, his birthplace. He holds an M.F.A. in p
 hotography from Yale University\, where he currently teaches.Kha's work i
 s in the collections of MoMA\, SFMoMA\, George Eastman House\, the Guggen
 heim Museum\, and the Virginia Museum of Fine Arts. His first solo museum
  show\, "Other Things Uttered\," was held at the Addison Gallery of Ameri
 can Art in September 2025.In 2023\, Aperture published his first monograp
 h "Half\, Full\, Quarter" following his solo shows "Ghost Bites" and "Má
 \," an ongoing\, decade-long collaboration between the artist and his mot
 her. Kha's work has also appeared in The New York Times Magazine\, The Ne
 w Yorker\, and The Wall Street Journal as well as Hyperallergic\, Intervi
 ew\, McSweeney's\, Vice\, Pitchfork\, Southern Cultures\, Dazed\, Foam\, 
 Butt Magazine\, and Miranda July's "We Think Alone."Kha is previously a r
 ecipient of the Hayes Prize\, Next Step Award\, Foam Talent\, and NYSCA/N
 YFA Artist Fellow in Photography. He is a former resident at Pioneer Work
 s\, Lighthouse Works\, Kinosaito\, Light Work\, and BAXTER ST (née Camer
 a Club of New York).He has had solo shows at Higher Pictures (which he jo
 ined in 2022)\, BAXTER ST\, and Blue Sky Gallery. He has taught at the Ne
 w School and Rutgers University and is a critic at Yale University. Curre
 ntly\, Kha studies kung fu under Sifu Ken Lo.According to Kha\, he "takes
  after his great aunt\, who 'read too many books and went crazy'." Ar
 tist's website:https://tommykha.com (https://tommykha.com)  &#160\;
